{"id": "EUVD-2026-76291", "enisaUuid": "875abbc1-696d-3f2d-8e84-ee8257a7c3d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: mts64: Check card index validity at probe\n\nAlthough mts64 driver has a check of the given devptr->id value, it\ndoesn't check for a negative id, which is often given as \"none\" or\nsuch value when bound via sysfs.  This may lead to OOB access for\nindex[] and other parameters.\n\nAdd a sanity check for the card index and warn/correct it if it's a\nvalue out of the range.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1566ca99fc0e892b9164ad893d268b00064fff54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d986d8c9e616636032636d99133f2535f94300d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5168a6241e953ecadb0ec05609649f6a7367fef8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cd7c59a106e7267d0cbcf68670594584d8689d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/036e7aa793375ab16ea0f64b8de6673220416cc1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4e774eeb61aec64da5b03d3becffde26f7fe4de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf3af453a48c8d905512dfc44a5a59439b70f4f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d18a260720f86a5f8b5fcfefc4ba2e9dd01c10f8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x5g7-h5wf-2v48", "CVE-2026-80968"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0533ef63-131a-3714-88ea-ec6c4a49136f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68ab801e32bbe2caac8b8c6e6e94f41fe7d687ad <5168a6241e953ecadb0ec05609649f6a7367fef8"}, {"id": "1c6fb735-458f-3321-8822-4a40205da35c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "207c5962-5375-3f03-a771-ba070bef1951", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "3fc44a39-e1f8-3458-96d7-d7430e1249d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6